research_rationale:
EO 13278 established the President's Commission on the United States Postal Service. Section 5 set a report deadline of July 31, 2003, which is a deadline and not an end. Section 6(b) states: "(b) The Commission shall terminate 30 days after submitting its report 
and in no event later than August 30, 2003." The fixed outer date of August 30, 2003 is the order's own first end, and it precedes the express revocation by EO 13316, effective September 30, 2003. The report-relative termination is an earlier possibility whose trigger date (the actual report submission) is not held anywhere in the repository, so it is disclosed and not recorded. Searches of held texts by the order's number found only the order's own copies and EO 13316.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Own terms: section 6(b) supplies a fixed outer end of August 30, 2003 (recorded inclusive; the exclusive reading is that the order ended when that day began). The report-relative thirty-day termination could have come earlier but its trigger date is not held; disclosed. Section 5 (report by July 31, 2003) is a deadline, not an end. No earlier revocation or supersession is held; EO 13316 (effective September 30, 2003) is later.","independent_command_check":"Section 4(g) (non-impairment of OMB functions) and section 6(a) (no private rights) create no independent continuing command; every other provision establishes, staffs, directs or reports from the Commission.","savings_check":"No saving provision appears in EO 13316 for EO 13278, and the order's commands were exhausted by the Commission's termination.","scope_check":"The inventory is the 20 scopes the packet derives from the Federal Register text of EO 13278 (67 FR 76671). Every scope serves the single Commission (section 4(g) and section 6(a) are construction and no-rights statements within the same order), so the Commission's own-terms end closes all of them on the same date."}
